 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Listen first without getting upset. Then ask if she's done her part as guest. Ask her politely to help while she's there, and keep the times short. Hmm, it feels bit like an excuse, I admit. What matters is making the times short and asking for help. Then ask about her day first, then bring up your job. Keep it about her too, like how she handles pressure. Some will, sadly. ignoring the criticising parts and focusing on the times she helps can help a lot. Let her finish, and then ask politely if she minds putting it back. Then it' worth considering keeping her opinion in mind when you organize again. Don't let it stop you from asking for help, though.",
